{"id":30,"date":"2022-11-21T12:25:36","date_gmt":"2022-11-21T12:25:36","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/?post_type=projects&#038;p=30"},"modified":"2025-06-03T06:52:17","modified_gmt":"2025-06-03T06:52:17","slug":"sacred-heart-primary-school-fitzroy-junior-school-renovations","status":"publish","type":"projects","link":"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/project\/sacred-heart-primary-school-fitzroy-junior-school-renovations\/","title":{"rendered":"Sacred Heart School"},"content":{"rendered":"\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate project-info\">\n        <div class=\"grid\">\n            <div class=\"grid__details\"\">\n\n                \n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Location<\/h5>\n                            <p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Fitzroy, Victoria<\/span><\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Client name<\/h5>\n                            <p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Melbourne Archdiocese Catholic Schools (MACS)<\/span><\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Value<\/h5>\n                            <p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">$1.44 MIL<\/span><\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Timeframe<\/h5>\n                            <p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">2020-2022<\/span><\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Contractor name<\/h5>\n                            <p><p><a href=\"http:\/\/www.stokesrousseau.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Stokes Rousseau<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Consultant team<\/h5>\n                            <p><p>Structural &amp; Civil Engineer &#8211; <a href=\"http:\/\/www.adamseng.com.au\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Adams Consulting Engineers<\/a><br \/>\nServices Engineer &#8211; <a href=\"http:\/\/www.njmdesign.com.au\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NJM Design<\/a><br \/>\nQuantity Surveyor &#8211; <a href=\"http:\/\/www.prowseqs.com.au\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Prowse Quantity Surveyors<\/a><br \/>\nBuilding Surveyor &#8211; <a href=\"http:\/\/www.duchateauchun.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">du Chateau Chun<\/a><\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Photographer<\/h5>\n                            <p><p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.yelp.com\/biz\/christopher-alexander-photography-blackburn\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Christopher Alexander Photography<\/a><\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                \n                \n                \n                                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"grid__text\">\n                <p>Our redesign of Sacred Heart Primary School saw the respectful evolution of this historic education facility to meet the growing needs of its diverse community and contemporary learners. The result is a hard-working building that provides an enjoyable and uplifting learning environment.<\/p>\n<p>In late 2018, we were commissioned to develop a master plan that reimagined the circulation and functioning of this complex, crowded and resource-challenged Catholic primary school in historic Fitzroy, Melbourne\u2019s first suburb.<\/p>\n<p>We recognised that the School\u2019s current configuration had evolved over decades and was poorly serving its staff and its diverse community including a high migrant, refugee and low-socio economic student population. The new master plan provides the school with a contemporary, secure, generous and welcoming entry point, with associated community facilities. Staff areas have been consolidated to provide an efficient and professional work environment. As part of a staged redevelopment process, we are introducing contemporary flexible learning spaces into the existing building, which was designed to accommodate traditional classrooms.<\/p>\n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate two-columns-image\">\n        <div class=\"grid\">\n            <div class=\"grid__image\">\n               <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"619\" height=\"821\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9483-1-7.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"Sacred Heart School colorful carpeted learning area\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9483-1-7.jpg 619w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9483-1-7-226x300.jpg 226w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 619px) 100vw, 619px\" \/>                           <\/div>\n            <div class=\"grid__image\">\n            <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"620\" height=\"821\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9318-1-7.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"Sacred Heart School open lockers\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9318-1-7.jpg 620w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9318-1-7-227x300.jpg 227w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px\" \/>                        <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed alignwide is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<iframe loading=\"lazy\" title=\"Sacred Heart Primary School, Fitzroy (School modernisation project)\" width=\"640\" height=\"360\" src=\"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/embed\/MlFHfShCJIk?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen><\/iframe>\n<\/div><\/figure>\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate full-width-image\">\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1320\" height=\"879\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9470-1-10.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9470-1-10.jpg 1320w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9470-1-10-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9470-1-10-1024x682.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9470-1-10-768x511.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1320px) 100vw, 1320px\" \/>    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate block-quote\">\n        <div class=\"max-sm:w-full ml-auto w-1\/2\">\n            <div>\n                <blockquote>\n\n                <p>Our design responds to the constraints of the once industrial nature of the site and the original, traditional teaching environment.<\/p>\n\n                \n                <\/blockquote>\n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate two-thirds-image\">\n        <div class=\"grid\">\n            <div>\n                <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"853\" height=\"569\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9574-1-10.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"Sacred Heart Primary School, lockers on the lobby\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9574-1-10.jpg 853w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9574-1-10-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9574-1-10-768x512.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 853px) 100vw, 853px\" \/>            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate two-columns-text-image\">\n        \n        \n        \n        \n        <div class=\"grid mt-[30px] md:mt-[50px]\">\n\n            <div class=\"grid__text space-y-12\">\n                                <div><p>Taking a lead from the school\u2019s stated desire to remove the inflexible and closed-in classroom formats and barbed-wire-topped fencing, we adopted a range of simple architectural approaches. We opened up and connected teaching spaces with large format sliding doors to encourage structured interaction and collaboration between classes and enable team teaching. We decluttered the corridor space to enable teaching spaces to break out into a shared zone. We designed colourful joinery and floor finishes to give spaces their own identities and establish clear paths of travel. We installed new palisade perimeter fencing, replacing the barbed wire fencing and its negative stigma.<\/p>\n<p>The junior playground was completely rebuilt with colourful and safer surfaces for running and play. The ground floor learning space was opened out into the playground with colourful flooring running from the indoor to the outdoor learning zone, complete with outdoor black\/whiteboard. A targeted range of play equipment and other discovery learning-based equipment such as built in musical instruments and a water-play zone add vital multi-purpose use to the playground, so critical due to the school\u2019s spatial restrictions.<\/p>\n<p>The project was warmly received by the school community and recognised with the award of two commendations in the Association for Learning Environments 2022 Awards Program; Category 6 Modernisation &#8211; Small, and Category 7 Small projects under $2 million. Sacred Heart Primary School shows that a design process that includes careful consideration of and consultation with those who use a space, can deliver an impactful building, no matter the budget.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n                            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"grid__image\">\n                 <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"620\" height=\"744\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9660-1-9.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"Sacred Heart School slides at the playground\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9660-1-9.jpg 620w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9660-1-9-250x300.jpg 250w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px\" \/>            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate full-width-image\">\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1320\" height=\"880\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9645-1-10.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"The front of Sacred Heart Primary School with trees and green rubber grass\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9645-1-10.jpg 1320w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9645-1-10-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9645-1-10-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9645-1-10-768x512.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1320px) 100vw, 1320px\" \/>    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate project-carousel\">\n\n        <div class=\"swiper swiper-block\">\n\n            \n                <div class=\"swiper-wrapper\">\n                    \n                                        \n                        <div class=\"swiper-slide\">\n                            <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"962\" height=\"641\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-5-1.png\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"Sacred Heart School indoor to outdoor view\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-5-1.png 962w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-5-1-300x200.png 300w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-5-1-768x512.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 962px) 100vw, 962px\" \/>                        <\/div>\n\n                                        \n                        <div class=\"swiper-slide\">\n                            <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"962\" height=\"641\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-7-1.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-7-1.jpg 962w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-7-1-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-7-1-768x512.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 962px) 100vw, 962px\" \/>                        <\/div>\n\n                                        \n                        <div class=\"swiper-slide\">\n                            <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"962\" height=\"641\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-8-1.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-8-1.jpg 962w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-8-1-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-8-1-768x512.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 962px) 100vw, 962px\" \/>                        <\/div>\n\n                                        \n                        <div class=\"swiper-slide\">\n                            <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"962\" height=\"641\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-9-1.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-9-1.jpg 962w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-9-1-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-9-1-768x512.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 962px) 100vw, 962px\" \/>                        <\/div>\n\n                                        \n                        <div class=\"swiper-slide\">\n                            <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"853\" height=\"568\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-10-e1673498217499.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-10-e1673498217499.jpg 853w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-10-e1673498217499-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/11\/69A9496-10-e1673498217499-768x511.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 853px) 100vw, 853px\" \/>                        <\/div>\n\n                                        \n                        <di